<h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mt-4">How to resize a signature to 10–20 KB for an online form</h1>
<p class="text-slate-600 mt-2 max-w-2xl">Many forms ask for a signature between 10 KB and 20 KB as JPEG. That is a range, not just a maximum: too small can also fail. Here is how to get a clean signature into that range, in your browser.</p>
<div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl bg-violet-50 border border-violet-200 p-4"><p class="text-slate-700 leading-relaxed"><strong>Signature 10–20 KB kaise kare?</strong> Safed kagaz par dark pen se sign karo, photo lo ya scan karo, phir signature tool me crop aur whitening se background saaf karo, aur size 10,240 se 20,480 bytes ke beech me check karo.</p></div>
<section class="card p-5 md:p-6 mt-8"><h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold">Steps</h2>
<ol class="list-decimal ml-6 mt-3 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
<li>Sign with a dark pen on plain white paper. Avoid ruled paper, shadows and coloured backgrounds — they make the file larger and harder to read.</li>
<li>Photograph or scan it in good, even light. Keep the signature large in the frame, with a small white margin around it.</li>
<li>Open the <a class="no-underline font-semibold text-violet-700 hover:text-violet-900" href="/tools/signature-10-to-20kb/">Signature Resize to 10–20 KB tool</a> and choose the image.</li>
<li>Use the crop control to cut out empty paper, turn on <strong>Whiten background</strong> if the paper looks grey, and adjust contrast until the strokes are dark and clear.</li>
<li>Tap <strong>Resize signature</strong> and check the preview and the actual byte size. It must be between 10,240 and 20,480 bytes.</li>
<li>Download, then re-check it in the <a class="no-underline font-semibold text-violet-700 hover:text-violet-900" href="/application-checker/">application checker</a> before submitting.</li>
</ol>
</section>
<section class="card p-5 md:p-6 mt-8"><h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold">If it will not reach 10 KB</h2>
<p class="mt-2 text-slate-700">A very small or faint signature may not contain enough detail to reach 10 KB, and the tool will say so rather than fake the size by padding the file. Try a larger, darker signature scan. Do not add random noise or a border just to increase the size — a form can still reject it for clarity.</p>
</section>
<section class="card p-5 md:p-6 mt-8"><h2 class="text-xl md:text-2xl font-bold">Common mistakes</h2>
<ul class="list-disc ml-6 mt-3 space-y-2 text-slate-700">
<li>Photographing a signature on a coloured or lined page.</li>
<li>Stretching the signature to fit a shape — this tool crops by percentage and does not stretch it.</li>
<li>Submitting a signature you cannot read in the preview, just because the size is right.</li>
</ul>
</section>
<p class="mt-6"><a class="btn w-full sm:w-auto" href="/tools/signature-10-to-20kb/">Resize a signature to 10–20 KB →</a></p>
<p class="mt-4 text-sm text-slate-500">This tool checks size and format only. It does not verify handwriting, identity or authenticity, and resizing does not guarantee acceptance.</p>
